From 213584a702492eef6e367ef991cbf453b8fb4e82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Konstantin Meshkov <skyline@mail.ru>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:46:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: marvell: add LED support for 88E1116R PHY

The Marvell 88E1116R PHY (used e.g. on the D-Link DNS-325) exposes its
LEDs through the same page 3 register 0x10 LED control layout as the
88E1318S: four bits of function-select per LED for LED[0..2], with the
same family function codes (OFF=0x8, ON=0x9, BLINK=0xb).  The stock
value 0x1107 programs LED0 = 1G link (mode 0x7) and LED2 = link/activity
(mode 0x1), leaving LED1 unused.

Wire up the existing 88E1318S LED handlers in the 88E1116R driver entry
so the PHY LEDs can be described in the device tree and driven through
the LED trigger API with hardware offload.  The DNS-325 device tree
change follows in a separate commit.

Signed-off-by: Konstantin Meshkov <skyline@mail.ru>

---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/marvell.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/marvell.c
@@ -3942,6 +3942,11 @@ static struct phy_driver marvell_drivers
 		.get_stats = marvell_get_stats,
 		.get_tunable = m88e1011_get_tunable,
 		.set_tunable = m88e1011_set_tunable,
+		.led_brightness_set = m88e1318_led_brightness_set,
+		.led_blink_set = m88e1318_led_blink_set,
+		.led_hw_is_supported = m88e1318_led_hw_is_supported,
+		.led_hw_control_set = m88e1318_led_hw_control_set,
+		.led_hw_control_get = m88e1318_led_hw_control_get,
 	},
 	{
 		.phy_id = MARVELL_PHY_ID_88E1510,
